WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
In 2016, the European Commission
fined truck makers a total

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.480
of 2.93 billion euros.

3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.190
They had colluded on prices,

4
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:13.540
from 1997 to 2011, instead of competing.

5
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.330
Yet in many markets with
only a few big firms,

6
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.490
prices move together
with no meeting at all.

7
00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.210
So when only a few big
firms share a market,

8
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.270
why do their prices so
often move together?

9
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.000
In this mission, you'll
see how a cartel tries

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.240
to act like a single monopoly.

11
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.320
Then you'll test, in a graph lab,

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.420
whether breaking the cartel's deal pays.

13
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.760
Your mission: explain why
a few big firms' prices

14
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.670
so often stay close together.
